    {
      "html" : "<\/div><\/div><div style=\"margin-bottom=10pt\">&#160;<\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-183052\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-183052\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\ta.&#160;&#160;&#160;The first two coats shall be as required for the first coats of exterior plaster, except that the moist-curing time period between the first and second coats shall not be less than 24 hours. Moist curing shall not be required where job and weather conditions are favorable to the retention of moisture in the cement plaster for the required time period.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-183053\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-183053\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tb.&#160;&#160;&#160;Twenty-four-hour minimum interval between coats of interior cement plaster. For alternate method of application, see Section 2512.8.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-183054\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-183054\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tc.&#160;&#160;&#160;Finish coat plaster is permitted to be applied to interior cement base coats after a 48-hour period.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><\/div>",
      "id" : "19045-html-3",
      "kind" : "html",
      "plainText" : "a. The first two coats shall be as required for the first coats of exterior plaster, except that the moist-curing time period between the first and second coats shall not be less than 24 hours. Moist curing shall not be required where job and weather conditions are favorable to the retention of moisture in the cement plaster for the required time period.\n\n b. Twenty-four-hour minimum interval between coats of interior cement plaster. For alternate method of application, see Section 2512.8.\n\n c. Finish coat plaster is permitted to be applied to interior cement base coats after a 48-hour period."
    }
